@baseUrl = http://localhost:5260

### 1. Start the source; Save intentionally fails after both parallel branches finish
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/runs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "delaySeconds": 5 }

> {% client.global.set("sourceId", response.body.sourceInstanceId); %}

### 2. Repeat until status is Failed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/runs/{{sourceId}}

### 3. Inspect source worker executions (Validate schedule before Inventory, completes later)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/executions?instanceId={{sourceId}}

### 4. Inspect native history, including completion-to-schedule references
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/runs/{{sourceId}}/history

### 5. Rerun from Inventory's actual native scheduling event; no input override
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/runs/{{sourceId}}/rerun-inventory

> {% client.global.set("rerunId", response.body.rerunInstanceId); %}

### 6. Repeat until status is Completed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/runs/{{rerunId}}

### 7. Prove which activity results were reused and which were newly produced
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compare?source={{sourceId}}&rerun={{rerunId}}

### 8. Worker executions under the new instance ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/executions?instanceId={{rerunId}}

### Optional: rerun from another native scheduling event (replace 0 with a listed ID)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/runs/{{sourceId}}/rerun
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": 0 }

> {% client.global.set("rerunId", response.body.rerunInstanceId); %}
